      "text": "BKN301 was a Banking-as-a-Service (BaaS) platform: a single, provider-\nagnostic banking backend that many products could be built on top of. This\ndiagram is my own design-level view of the whole system, meant as a map to\nskim before zooming into any single component (e.g. 301core).\n\nIt reads top-down as a hierarchy. Two visual conventions carry most of\nthe meaning: a dashed container is a monorepo — one team's codebase that\ngroups many services — and each solid box inside it is an individually\ndeployed service (an API).\n\nAt the top sits 301gateway: a set of presentation gateways, one tailored\nper product — the retail app (301wallet), the merchant acquiring platform\n(301pay), a dedicated gateway for the Hype integration, the internal\nadmin/ops console (301admin), and per-customer gateways (301xxx) for\nbespoke integrations such as a Bitcoin-card provider or a client plugging\nour APIs into their ERP.\n\nUnderneath, the platform splits into two monorepos. 301core holds the\nhardcore banking systems — AML (KYC/KYB/KYT), Bank Accounts,\nPayments, Cards and PoS — each one an abstraction that plugs into\nmultiple interchangeable providers. 301services holds the non-banking add-\nons everything else leans on — Authentication, Alias, Notification and\nDocuments.\n\nThe leaf level is the provider / datastore each service depends on: every\nservice talks to at least two of them — which is exactly what the\nabstractions above are designed to hot-swap.",
      "fontSize": 17.7,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "BKN301 was a Banking-as-a-Service (BaaS) platform: a single, provider-agnostic banking backend that many products could be built on top of. This diagram is my own design-level view of the whole system, meant as a map to skim before zooming into any single component (e.g. 301core).\n\nIt reads top-down as a hierarchy. Two visual conventions carry most of the meaning: a dashed container is a monorepo — one team's codebase that groups many services — and each solid box inside it is an individually deployed service (an API).\n\nAt the top sits 301gateway: a set of presentation gateways, one tailored per product — the retail app (301wallet), the merchant acquiring platform (301pay), a dedicated gateway for the Hype integration, the internal admin/ops console (301admin), and per-customer gateways (301xxx) for bespoke integrations such as a Bitcoin-card provider or a client plugging our APIs into their ERP.\n\nUnderneath, the platform splits into two monorepos. 301core holds the hardcore banking systems — AML (KYC/KYB/KYT), Bank Accounts, Payments, Cards and PoS — each one an abstraction that plugs into multiple interchangeable providers. 301services holds the non-banking add-ons everything else leans on — Authentication, Alias, Notification and Documents.\n\nThe leaf level is the provider / datastore each service depends on: every service talks to at least two of them — which is exactly what the abstractions above are designed to hot-swap.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "a0116V",
      "autoResize": false
    },
